{"title":"2025 TMTA High School Algebra II Contest Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_II_Contest_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For what length radius would the value of the surface area of a sphere (in square units) be triple the value of the volume (in cubic units) of the same sphere?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/4/cf431904eb0f9ca0faa08aec545d88e5ce887783.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ r = 1 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ r = \\frac{4}{9} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ r = 4 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ r = 12 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ r = \\frac{4}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"533\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_II_Contest_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the radius of the sphere. The surface area would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/5/67509ec0e4350b804add97a39d59431f82d19e35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times \\pi \\times r^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" /> and the volume would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/b/c1b072fa0d64d5dc589a4ab0e7a69910f38375d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{3} \\times \\pi \\times r^{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"38\" />. If the surface area is triple the volume, then we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/8/1c8d005120bb2cad89ac45b0eb0f8fdd1a6346e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times \\pi \\times r^{2} = \\frac{4}{3} \\times \\pi \\times r^{3} \\times 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"223\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/6/b3692dff27c6d6b08e8d1b63e0a192e4fec058cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times \\pi \\times r^{2} = 4 \\times \\pi \\times r^{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"187\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/3/ca384b5cfcf30ef8f2512d0508db864e0cd351fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4 \\times \\pi \\times r^{3}}{4 \\times \\pi \\times r^{2}} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"120\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/6/45670d7744069e3b529db072c318213150922e4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(A) } r = 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"91\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_II_Contest\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra II Contest\">2025 TMTA Algebra II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_II_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra II Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_II_Contest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra II Contest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\"